{
  "about": [
    "Which word and which light a header shows, as test vectors (v0.6.10, F5). One rule, held against",
    "three implementations by tests/test_light_parity.py: the popup (ui/popup/model.py activity and",
    "light_for), the Codex panel (mcp/assets/panel.js activity and lightFor, run in Node) and the settings",
    "window (gui/DashboardActions.cs ActivityWord and Activity, compiled with csc).",
    "",
    "Each vector is what a surface read - get_status (`status`, null when it could not be read) and",
    "list_pending (`rows`, null when it could not be read) - at `now`, and the header's `word`",
    "(activity.<word> in the catalogs) and `light` (the status dot, brand.STATUS_FILL). The rule, in order:",
    "  1. no status, or a watcher not known to be running - the status does not say it runs, or a row is held",
    "     for a watcher that is not (engine_unavailable, read a moment apart from the status): the word asks for",
    "     attention, the light is idle grey, never a moving light beside a watcher called stopped;",
    "  2. a watcher that runs but is not well - an older watcher still owns the state, it is not ticking, the",
    "     engine is incompatible or failed here, or a row is held for one of those - is attention, amber;",
    "  3. recovery not known to be on is paused;",
    "  4. a row sent into Codex (a code in `moving`), or a status count of one, is recovering;",
    "  5. a waiting row whose time has come is checking;",
    "  6. any other row, or a status count of any, is waiting;",
    "  7. otherwise monitoring.",
    "The light is the word, except under rule 1.",
    "",
    "`panel` is where the panel differs, and only by rule 5: it is drawn once from one tool result and never",
    "redrawn, so it has no clock to say a time has come by; it says waiting, beside each row's 'due now'.",
    "",
    "`taskbar` is the window's taskbar button (SettingsForm.TrayActivity), which follows the notification-area",
    "icon's own rule and not this one: it is given only to show that a failure nobody has seen is red there",
    "and nowhere in a header. The icon's rule is not held to this table."
  ],
